1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,440
My husband agreed to sell our house in two seconds flat. That bottle of perfume changed everything.

2
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:14,532
For five years, Mark fought me on every single choice. Now, he just smiles and nods.

3
00:00:14,832 --> 00:00:22,992
The salesclerk called it absolute alignment. One spray behind the ear, and resistance simply vanished.

4
00:00:23,292 --> 00:00:30,204
At work, my boss usually rips my ideas to shreds. Today, he gave me a standing ovation.

5
00:00:30,504 --> 00:00:36,864
Even the barista who hates me poured my coffee with a worshipful bow. It felt incredible.

6
00:00:37,164 --> 00:00:42,828
Power is a warm drug. But tonight, I noticed something strange about the radio announcer.

7
00:00:43,128 --> 00:00:51,600
He was speaking live, debating politics. But his lips moved, and the studio speakers repeated my exact thoughts.

8
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:57,876
I grabbed Mark's shoulders and begged him to yell at me. Just scream, please! Anything!

9
00:00:58,176 --> 00:01:04,224
He just smiled wider, whispering that I was always right. The perfume didn't change them at all.

10
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:09,636
It didn't make them agree. It just deafened me to every voice that dared to differ.
